WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.243
Riders online now has a lobby: it seats you in a live race and counts down with

00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:08.428
everyone in it.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.200
From level three, Race Setup counts the riders queuing for the map, and Find a race

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.440
opens the lobby.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.037
The service seats you in the fullest open race on the map, or opens one that starts

00:00:28.037 --> 00:00:29.554
thirty seconds later.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.800
Riders come and go as it happens; when one leaves, their seat opens again and the

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.964
lobby says who.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.768
At ten seconds, bots take every open seat so the race starts full, and the first

00:00:53.768 --> 00:00:56.315
stretch's resistance goes to the bike.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.697
On a laptop the clock sits beside the grid; on a phone the grid runs underneath.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.740
What the tests prove: seated by the hub, the grid in step for everyone, bots at ten,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.904
and your seat freed when you go.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
